---
code: cli-file-permission-denied
when-fires: an input file exists but this process may not read it. cli/lib.rs humane_read_error, PermissionDenied arm. {kind} and {path}.
why: the read-error trichotomys second arm: the file is there, so the repair is permissions, not the path - a distinction the raw OS string buries.
edit-loop: edit a sentence in the transcript below, then run `mise run loom:compile -- cli-file-permission-denied && mise run loom:promote -- cli-file-permission-denied`. `mise run loom:vars -- --all cli-file-permission-denied` lists this case's values; type {{name}} to insert or move one.
---
-- replay --
$ dorc plan --book=webhost.sh
error[cli-file-permission-denied]: sm cannot read oracle
`/etc/dorc/nginx.oracle.sh`: permission denied
